> that's why I need to check the configuration of the FW interface, 
> that should act as boot PROM at that address...

The LSI-11 system I used to use didn't have a ROM at 173000, but
the AED floppy disk controller faked it.  The disk controller 
could read the boot block into memory.  It would generate a
 jump .   (or the PDP-11 equivalent) until the boot block was
read in, then generate a jump to the read in block.  So no actual ROM.

-- glen


