    Often, when someone's box has, or seems to have, died,
I see them getting lots of "bad power supply" comments.
While that frequently turns out to be the problem,
it even more frequently turns out to be something else
entirely (unless, of course, it's visually obvious something's
"fried"). I've kind of concluded that while power's indeed one
of the first things to check, you probably don't want to focus
on it to the exclusion of other possibilities.
    After swapping 60<-->90 supplies from a perfectly working
