One trick is there are HVD->Single Ended converters you can buy
to convert the bus levels.  I used one on my HP 300mb scsi drive...
50 pin SE in --> 50 pin HVD out.  Worked great to let me get FreeBSD and
SimH up about 15 years ago.

Converting the bus (or part of it) may work and be easier than finding
a correct HVD controller for an unusual platform.

Remember -- SCSI is SCSI -- the difference between HVD and LVD is
voltage levels (bus drivers).

Bill

