John, a workaround like this does ignore the problem which may
increase in severity.
I agree that the power supply is not suspect. Neither is the main
board because otherwise you'd have seen an error message before
getting at the SRM prompt. With the system switched off, put a little
pressure on one of the long sides of the power connector on the main
board. Just push it with one hand and power on the VAX. If there's no
change, repeat the procedure but apply pressure on the opposite side.
